Ticket **#4471** was marked known as one parser bug. The export's own cause rules disagree:
**412** unique reports cover **two** causes that share the same wrong-day symptom.

<Callout>
Split #4471. One ticket per cause. Counts below come from the live table, not typed in.
</Callout>

## What #4471 really holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Tickets to open

| cause | reports | problem |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `parser` | 379 | Shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get the month and day flipped. |
| `hint` | 33 | `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. The tenant still reads day first, so the form and the person disagree. |

Five reports under `parser` were also read at the desk as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`); they stay filed by tenant cause.

## Why the merge was wrong

Intake tags and subject-line dedupe both group by how the report *sounds*. Cause depends on the tenant's locale and which booking form they run (`causes.ts`). Subject match put two bugs in one ticket.

The desk view of this page (static render) sits at [`/desk-view/4471-split.html`](/desk-view/4471-split.html) in the repo root.

